<!--
  ZA.Mediator v7.0.0 - intentional API breaks for the major version bump.

  PKV006 net8.0: every runtime package now targets net10.0 and net11.0 only. .NET 8 went out of
  support in November 2026, so the net8.0 assets are dropped. One entry covers all six packages.

  CP0001 MediatorBuilderExtensions, #277: RegisterHandlersFromAssembly and
  RegisterHandlersFromAssemblies have been [Obsolete] since 6.2 and are removed together with the
  class that held them. The generated AddMediator() registers every handler at compile time;
  docs/migrating-to-v7.md gives the replacement.

  Pipeline state, #463: the provider of the request is now the state of every behavior's Handle,
  so the generated IMediator.Send chain is static and allocates no delegate per behavior.
  CP0002 Handle<TRequest, TResponse> on AuthorizationBehavior, CacheBehavior, ResilienceBehavior,
  TelemetryBehavior and ValidationBehavior: replaced by Handle<TRequest, TResponse, TState>, the
  state being the last type parameter and the second argument. CP0002 on the second Handle
  overload that took an IServiceProvider, CP0001 PipelineBehaviorServices and CP0002
  PipelineBehaviorAttribute.UsesPipelineBehaviorServices: all three are removed, because the
  state carries the provider and the AsyncLocal write behind PipelineBehaviorServices allocated
  72 B per Send. docs/migrating-to-v7.md has the migration.

  Generated by apicompat in suppression-file mode against the 6.7.2 baseline of each package. Only
  these breaks are listed, so an accidental removal elsewhere still fails the job.

  Diagnostic-ID reference:
  https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/fundamentals/package-validation/diagnostic-ids
-->
